// MLX Codemap: the code base as a space to fly through. Every folder is a
// group with its files around it, every file has its declarations around
// it (functions, structs, enums, constants, variables, tests), structs
// their fields and functions; lines show what belongs where and what
// imports what. Select something and the lines show what it connects to:
// what it calls, uses or imports (cyan) and what calls, uses or imports
// it (orange), listed in the panel on the right with its signature and
// doc comment. Laid out like the file manager (examples/mlx-files): the
// groups in a translucent sidebar, back and forward, the name and a
// search field in the toolbar, where it is in the status bar.
//
//   mlx-codemap [ROOT]          the 3D view of ROOT (default:
//                               MLX_CODEMAP_ROOT, else the Git work tree
//                               around the working directory)
//   mlx-codemap COMMAND ...     the command line (tools/codemap/main.mlx)
//
// Drawn on the GPU: the canvas draws the panels and labels, a compute
// shader (scene_shader.mlx) the spheres, glows and lines under them;
// without Vulkan the same picture is drawn on the CPU.
//
// The mouse: dragging turns the view, with the right button (or Shift) it
// moves, the wheel comes closer or goes away; a click selects, a double
// click flies there. The keyboard: typing searches (Enter or a click flies
// to a result), Escape clears the search, then the selection, then goes
// up a group; Enter flies to what is selected, Alt+Up to its group,
// Backspace or Alt+Left goes back, Alt+Right forward, the arrows turn,
// +/- come closer and go away, Ctrl+O opens the selection in the editor
// (MLX_EDITOR, else VS Code, else xdg-open), F5 reads the code again,
// Ctrl+W closes.
const std = @import("std")
const vk = @import("std.vulkan")
